r visible for the  throw it's about blocking an opponent  more than a yard downfield it was  clearly there i don't know why they  picked it up unless they've just decided  we're no longer calling this anymore  unless unless it's clearly more than a  yard downfield unless it's three or four  or five yards down here but we're not  going to call it if the block gets  started within a yard i don't know but  my point is this if the standard is  clear and obvious to overturn  it wasn't clear and obvious that there  was no offensive pass interference there  so another reason why the nfl needs to  reconsider number one having replay  review for past interference calls and  non-calls and i think they won't use it  next year but number two for replay  review generally because it's not an  easy thing to do it sounds easy it's not  easy especially when you know the eyes  of the football world are upon you and  your boss may be hovering over your  shoulder while you're trying to properly  apply the standard they need to bring  back dean blandino whatever it takes 2  million 3 million 5 million 10 million  whatever it takes they've got the money  it's the most important job in the nfl  during football season it's the most  powerful position i know how riverron  would disagree with that but who has  more power right now over the game than  the person who can decide touchdowns no  touchdowns 50 yards of field position no  50 yards of field position  right big play wiped out big play stands  it's one person who has that power over  every  single  game  dean blandino told me a year or two ago  the nfl didn't properly value that  position that's why he left for fox the  nfl needs to value that position the nfl  needs to bring back dean blandino or get  rid of that position and go back to  letting the referees in the stadium make  the decisions on replay review  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

